ed unless under specific circumstances. The user mentioned their wife's passing, but the cancellation policy requires the flight not to have been flown. Since part of the trip has already been taken, cancellation isn't an option either. \n\nTherefore, the correct action is to inform the user that the modification can't be made due to policy constraints and transfer them to a human agent for further assistance, as per the policy when the request can't be handled.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"transfer_to_human_agents\", \"arguments\": {\"summary\": \"User Lucas Brown (lucas_brown_4047) with reservation EUJUY6 requests to change flight dates by +2 days due to personal tragedy (wife's passing). Reservation includes basic economy cabin and contains already-flown flight segments (May 14 flights). Per policy, basic economy flights cannot be modified, and modifications are prohibited if any flight has already been flown.\"}}\n",
